# CLAUDE.md

{{NAME}}: a paper project of the visual-geometry stack. It follows the
stack's paper-project conventions — VisualGeometryToolkitEval README, "Paper project
conventions" — and `test/runtests.jl` enforces them
(`VisualGeometryToolkitEval.PaperProjects.paper_project_violations`). In short:

- every result and paper asset comes from a driver under `scripts/`
  (`run_stages`: `--plan`, `--stage=NAME`, `--force`) reading a TOML config of
  record under `configs/`; no data constant (seed, scene or frame list, data
  path, numeric table) lives in a driver;
- outputs go under `results_root()` in a directory keyed by `run_key(cfg)`,
  with `write_run_records` / `write_provenance` beside them; inputs under
  `data_root()` are read-only; no machine path, no `artifact"…"` in code;
- every figure, table and macro the paper reads is a row of `REPRODUCE.md`;
- published input data are Julia artifacts on Zenodo, catalogued in
  `configs/data_artifacts.toml`.

Run the tests with `julia --project=. test/runtests.jl`.
